EVALUATION.md §1, CODEGEN.md §5.1: gen/go writes a list constant as a Go composite literal, which cannot hold a record of another package (its fields are unexported there), so the constant is CrossPackageBakedValue in baked mode.
-- b/b.canon --
package b

/// A point.
record Point {
  /// Across.
  x: Int
}

emit go { out: "@features/b", package: "b" }
-- a/a.canon --
package a

import b { Point }

/// The origins.
const origins = [Point { x: 0 }]

/// Numbers, fine.
const ns = [1, 2]

emit go { out: "@features/a", package: "a" }
-- a.origins.json --
[{"x": 0}]
-- a.ns.json --
[1, 2]
-- findings.txt --
error[E8019]  a/a.canon:6:7
  emit go in baked mode cannot generate a value of a record, variant or table of another package

1 error, 0 warnings in 2 packages (…)
